IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `er4-nouns`
IMPORT `er4-part2-national-employment-service`
IMPORT `er4-part3-reduction`
IMPORT `er4-part3-reg63-weekly-indemnity-plan`
IMPORT `er4-part3-regs64-66-other-plans`
IMPORT `er4-part3-qualifying-plan`
IMPORT `er4-part3-application`
IMPORT `er4-part3-1-premium-reduction`
IMPORT `er4-part3-1-entitlement`
IMPORT `er4-part3-1-weeks`
IMPORT `er4-part3-1-premiums-and-administration`
IMPORT `er4-part3-2-self-employed`

-- Employment Insurance Regulations (SOR/96-332), Parts II, III, III.1 and III.2 (regs 58 to 76.45): THE SEAT LAYER, piece er4.
--
-- SEAT: a person who has lost work, or cannot work because of sickness, pregnancy, caring for a child or a family member,
-- or who is self-employed or a fisher, asking whether they qualify for Employment Insurance benefits, how many hours or
-- weeks they need, how much they would receive and for how long, and what they must do or tell the Commission. Officials
-- (the Commission, the Minister of National Revenue, the Canada Revenue Agency) have no seat; their duties and powers
-- appear here only as what the person is owed or exposed to. An employer's seat is not written in this piece.
--
-- WHERE THE PERSON'S QUESTIONS ARE. Part II gives the person a claim on the national employment service. Part III is about
-- the employer's premium and the employer's wage-loss plan; the person asks only whether the reduction is made in respect
-- of them, whether the plan meets its standards, what share of the reduction insured persons must benefit from, and
-- which category their premiums are in. Parts III.1 and III.2 carry most of the person's questions: whether provincial
-- benefits (such as QPIP) bar or reduce federal benefits, how provincial weeks count, how weeks are shared by two parents
-- in different provinces, and what premium is taken from them. The duties that bind only an employer or an official are
-- encoded in layer 1 and have no question here: reg 58(a), (d); regs 62(3), (4); regs 68 to 70 (except the category in
-- 69(1)), 72 to 76; regs 76.02, 76.03, 76.06, 76.07, 76.08, 76.27, 76.32, 76.35.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs (yes/no, numbers, dates, or a choice of the modules' own constructors),
-- one for each fact the person can state, each with an @desc worded as the person would be asked. The records and lists the
-- layer-1 modules expect are built inside each question, in its WHERE, from those answers, and the SAME module rule is then
-- called; no rule is restated. A record field that no rule called ever reads is given a fixed placeholder, with a comment
-- saying so. A judgment the text hands to the Commission or to the service ("where appropriate", "substantially
-- equivalent") is asked as a yes/no fact about that judgment and never decided here.
-- One question serves the employed ("insured") person and the self-employed person where Parts III.1 and III.2 say the same
-- thing (they are the same relation): it asks "Are you self-employed?" and calls the Part III.2 rule for them.
-- Figures of the Act that the formulas read (the 35 and 61 weeks of s 12(3)(b), the 40 of s 12(4)(b)(i), the maxima of s 12 and
-- s 152.14) are asked as numbers; they are the Act's, not this piece's (out of range: Act ss 12 and 152.14, pieces ei1 and ei5).

§ `Part II -- the national employment service`

-- Situation: anyone who works or wants to work. Reg 59: the service is free to all workers, whether insured or not and whether
-- claiming benefits or not, so neither fact is asked.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 59
@export Can I use the national employment service at no cost (reg 59)?
GIVEN `I work or want to work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you work, or are you looking for work?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I use the national employment service at no cost` IS
    `reg 59 the national employment service is to be made available at no cost to` `my kind of user`
    WHERE
        `my kind of user` MEANS IF `I work or want to work` THEN `er4 a worker` ELSE `er4 someone else`

-- Reg 58(b): labour market information is to be made available to the general public, which includes the person.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 58(b)
@export Is the national employment service to make labour market information available to me (reg 58(b))?
GIVEN `I am a member of the general public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of the general public (anyone is, unless you are asking for an organization such as a public authority or an employers' or workers' organization)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the national employment service to make labour market information available to me` IS
    `reg 58(b) the national employment service is to make labour market information available systematically and promptly to` `my kind of recipient`
    WHERE
        `my kind of recipient` MEANS IF `I am a member of the general public` THEN `er4 a member of the general public` ELSE `er4 someone else`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 58(c)(i)
@export Is the national employment service to give me information on job openings and on careers in demand (reg 58(c)(i))?
GIVEN `I am a worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a worker (do you work, or look for work)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the national employment service to give me information on job openings and on careers in demand` IS
    `reg 58(c)(i) the national employment service is to make available information on employment opportunities and on careers and occupations in demand to` `I am a worker`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 58(c)(ii)
@export Is the national employment service to refer me to other sources of labour market information (reg 58(c)(ii))?
GIVEN `I am a worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a worker (do you work, or look for work)?
      `the service considers it appropriate to refer me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the national employment service consider it appropriate to refer you to other sources of labour market information, such as social service agencies?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the national employment service to refer me to other sources of labour market information` IS
    `reg 58(c)(ii) the national employment service is to refer a worker to other sources of labour market information` `I am a worker` `the service considers it appropriate to refer me`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 58(c)(iii)
@export May the national employment service obtain from me the information it needs to refer me to jobs (reg 58(c)(iii))?
GIVEN `I am a worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a worker (do you work, or look for work)?
      `I am seeking employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you seeking employment?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the national employment service obtain from me the information it needs to refer me to jobs` IS
    `reg 58(c)(iii) the national employment service is to obtain from a worker the information necessary to effect proper referrals` `I am a worker` `I am seeking employment`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 58(c)(iv)
@export Is the national employment service to interview and counsel me and help me make an action plan (reg 58(c)(iv))?
GIVEN `I am a worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a worker (do you work, or look for work)?
      `local strategies call for interviewing and counselling me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the local community-based service and client targeting strategies call for interviewing and counselling you?
      `it is necessary to interview and counsel me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it necessary to interview and counsel you to assess your employment needs?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the national employment service to interview and counsel me and help me make an action plan` IS
    `reg 58(c)(iv) the national employment service is to interview and counsel a worker and help them develop action plans` `I am a worker` `local strategies call for interviewing and counselling me` `it is necessary to interview and counsel me`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 58(c)(v)
@export Is the national employment service to tell me about special assistance (reg 58(c)(v))?
GIVEN `I am a worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a worker (do you work, or look for work)?
      `I am having particular difficulty obtaining or keeping employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you having particular difficulty obtaining or keeping employment?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the national employment service to tell me about special assistance` IS
    `reg 58(c)(v) the national employment service is to provide a worker with information on the availability of special assistance` `I am a worker` `I am having particular difficulty obtaining or keeping employment`

§ `Part III -- my employer's sick-leave or wage-loss plan`

-- Situation: only for a person whose employer has a wage-loss plan (a weekly indemnity plan or a paid sick leave plan) and
-- has applied, or may apply, for a reduction of the employer's premium. The employer applies and has the duties; these
-- questions are what the person can ask about the reduction and their own part in it.

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations regs 62(1), 62(2)
@export Is my employer's premium rate reduced because of me (regs 62(1), 62(2))?
GIVEN `my employer's plan covers me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your employer's wage-loss plan (sick pay or sickness-benefit plan) cover you?
      `my employer's plan meets the standards for its kind` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your employer's plan meet the standards of regulation 63, 64, 65 or 66 for its kind (see the question on the standards)?
      `my employer's plan is a qualifying plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employer's plan a qualifying plan (see the question on qualifying plans)?
      `my eligibility to use paid sick leave is deferred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your eligibility to use paid sick leave deferred under a cumulative or enhanced paid sick leave plan (for example because you are a temporary or probationary employee)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my employer's premium rate reduced because of me` IS
    `reg 62(1) the employer's premium rate is to be reduced in respect of the insured person`
        `my employer's plan covers me` `my employer's plan meets the standards for its kind` `my employer's plan is a qualifying plan` `my eligibility to use paid sick leave is deferred`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 61
@export By how much must the insured persons benefit from my employer's premium reduction, in dollars (reg 61)?
GIVEN `the reduction of my employer's premium` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the reduction of your employer's premium, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `By how much must the insured persons benefit from my employer's premium reduction` IS
    `reg 61 five-twelfths of the reduction of the employer's premium` `the reduction of my employer's premium`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 61
@export Does the Part on employers' wage-loss plans apply to me and my co-workers (reg 61)?
GIVEN `my employer's plan meets the standards of regulation 63, 64, 65 or 66 and covers us` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your employer's plan meet the standards of regulation 63, 64, 65 or 66, and does it cover you and your co-workers who are insured persons?
      `the reduction of my employer's premium` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the reduction of your employer's premium, in dollars?
      `the amount of the reduction that we benefit from` IS A NUMBER @desc How many dollars of that reduction do you and the other insured persons benefit from?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the Part on employers' wage-loss plans apply to me and my co-workers` IS
    `reg 61 this Part applies`
        `my employer's plan meets the standards of regulation 63, 64, 65 or 66 and covers us`
        `the reduction of my employer's premium` `the amount of the reduction that we benefit from`

-- Regs 63 to 66 in one question: the kind of plan decides which requirements are tested. The lists the layer-1 rules read
-- (the events that end payment, the conditions that preclude payment) are built from yes/no answers: a plan that stops
-- paying only at the events the paragraph names, or refuses payment only in the 17 cases of reg 63(g) within their limits,
-- answers "no" to the last three inputs.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations regs 63, 64, 65, 66
@export Does my employer's wage-loss plan meet the standards for its kind (regs 63, 64, 65, 66)?
GIVEN `the kind of my employer's plan` IS A `er4 Kind of wage-loss plan` @desc Which kind of plan is it: a Weekly Indemnity Plan, a Special Weekly Indemnity Plan, a Cumulative Paid Sick Leave Plan, an Enhanced Cumulative Paid Sick Leave Plan, or another wage-loss plan?
      `my plan is based on an hour-bank principle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your plan count hours of active employment (an hour-bank principle) rather than months?
      `the day my employment commenced` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your employment with this employer commence (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-01-15)?
      `the day I become eligible to claim benefits under my plan` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you become eligible to claim benefits under the plan for an illness or injury (ISO 8601)?
      `the day I have an accumulation of 400 hours of active employment` IS A DATE @desc If your plan counts hours: on what day do you have 400 hours of active employment (ISO 8601; any date if it does not count hours)?
      `my plan requires an elimination period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Must you serve an elimination period, during which no benefit is payable, before the plan pays?
      `the days in my plan's elimination period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many consecutive days is the elimination period (0 if none)?
      `the elimination period begins with the first day of my incapacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the elimination period begin with the first day of your period of incapacity due to illness or injury?
      `my plan pays in full whatever I am paid under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the plan pay its benefits in full whatever benefits you are paid under the Employment Insurance Act?
      `my plan pays in full whatever I am paid from another source that is not earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the plan pay its benefits in full whatever you are paid from another source that does not count as earnings under regulation 35?
      `the weekly benefit my plan pays me` IS A NUMBER @desc What weekly benefit does the plan pay you, in dollars?
      `my normal weekly insurable earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your normal weekly insurable earnings, in dollars?
      `the active employment after which my full benefits are reinstated when the illness recurs` IS A NUMBER @desc After how much active employment are your full benefits reinstated if the same illness or injury recurs: months, or hours if your plan counts hours?
      `the active employment after which my full benefits are reinstated for a new illness` IS A NUMBER @desc After how much active employment are your full benefits reinstated for a new illness or injury: months, or hours if your plan counts hours? For a special weekly indemnity plan, give the months after which full benefits are reinstated.
      `the longest period my plan pays benefits for one illness or injury, in weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc For a weekly indemnity plan: for how many weeks at most does the plan pay for one illness or injury?
      `my plan stops paying when my accumulated paid sick leave is exhausted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the plan stop paying when your accumulated paid sick leave is used up?
      `my plan stops paying at some other event` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the plan stop paying at any event other than the end of the benefit period, the end of your incapacity, your retirement, or your separation from employment (for a reason other than illness, notice having been given before the illness began)?
      `my plan refuses payment in a case reg 63(g) does not allow` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the plan refuse payment in any case other than these: you are not under a licensed physician's care; the illness or injury is covered by workers' compensation, the Canada Pension Plan or the Quebec Pension Plan (where the amounts count as earnings); is self-inflicted; results from armed forces service; from war or a riot; occurs during leave or paid vacation; you receive benefits under sections 22 to 23.3; occurs while committing a crime; you are working for pay during the period; you fell ill after losing work in a labour dispute (if your right is reinstated on return); you are in prison; you are not in Canada; the illness results from drugs or alcohol and you are not receiving continuing treatment; a motor vehicle accident covered by a provincial plan; you receive a retirement pension from the employer; cosmetic surgery (except where needed because of illness or injury); or a recurring disability for which you receive group long-term disability benefits with a reinstatement period of six months or less?
      `the employer providing or financing my plan` IS A `er4 Employer that provides or finances a plan` @desc For a special weekly indemnity plan: who provides or finances the plan: Her Majesty in right of a province, a provincial Crown corporation, a municipal authority, a public authority of a province, an institution primarily controlled, supported or financed by a province, or any other employer?
      `my plan credits only after the period or the hours in paragraph 63(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a paid sick leave plan: does it credit paid sick leave only after the period of continuous employment, or the hours, referred to in paragraph 63(a)?
      `the days of paid sick leave my plan credits for each full month` IS A NUMBER @desc For a paid sick leave plan: how many days of paid sick leave does it credit for each full month of active employment?
      `the days each month my plan keeps for illness, injury, pregnancy, child care or care of a family member` IS A NUMBER @desc For a paid sick leave plan: how many of those days each month are available only for your illness or injury, or while you are at home because of pregnancy or to care for a child or a family member?
      `the months for which my plan defers my eligibility to use paid sick leave` IS A NUMBER @desc For a paid sick leave plan: for how many months is your eligibility to use paid sick leave deferred (0 if it is not)?
      `my plan lets unused days accumulate at the credited rate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a paid sick leave plan: do unused days available for those purposes accumulate at the rate at which they are credited?
      `the most working days of paid sick leave my plan lets me accumulate` IS A NUMBER @desc For a paid sick leave plan: what is the most working days of paid sick leave you can accumulate?
      `the longest period my plan pays benefits for one illness or injury, in working days` IS A NUMBER @desc For a paid sick leave plan: for how many working days at most does the plan pay for one illness or injury?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my employer's wage-loss plan meet the standards for its kind` IF
    CONSIDER `the kind of my employer's plan`
    WHEN `er4 a Weekly Indemnity Plan` THEN `reg 63 the plan meets the requirements of a Weekly Indemnity Plan` `my section 63 case`
    WHEN `er4 a Special Weekly Indemnity Plan` THEN `reg 64 the plan meets the requirements of a Special Weekly Indemnity Plan` `my special weekly indemnity case`
    WHEN `er4 a Cumulative Paid Sick Leave Plan` THEN `reg 65 the plan meets the requirements of a Cumulative Paid Sick Leave Plan` `my cumulative case`
    WHEN `er4 an Enhanced Cumulative Paid Sick Leave Plan` THEN `reg 66 the plan meets the requirements of an Enhanced Cumulative Paid Sick Leave plan` `my enhanced case`
    OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHERE
        -- The four events the paragraphs name; the exhaustion of accumulated sick leave is added where the plan stops then,
        -- and "any other event" where it stops at another. Regs 63(f) and 64(d) do not allow the last two; regs 65(f) and 66(e)
        -- allow the exhaustion.
        `my events` MEANS
            append (LIST `er4 the end of a period during which the benefits are paid`
                       , `er4 the end of the period of incapacity due to the illness or injury`
                       , `er4 the date the insured person retires`
                       , `er4 the date of the insured person's separation from employment for a reason other than illness or injury, notice having been given before the onset of the illness or the occurrence of the injury`)
                   (append (IF `my plan stops paying when my accumulated paid sick leave is exhausted` THEN LIST `er4 the exhaustion of all accumulated paid sick leave` ELSE EMPTY)
                           (IF `my plan stops paying at some other event` THEN LIST `er4 any other event` ELSE EMPTY))
        `my conditions` MEANS
            IF `my plan refuses payment in a case reg 63(g) does not allow` THEN LIST `er4 a condition not listed in paragraph 63(g)` ELSE EMPTY
        `my section 63 case` MEANS `er4 Case under a Weekly Indemnity Plan` WITH
            `er4 plan based on an hour-bank principle` IS `my plan is based on an hour-bank principle`
            `er4 day the employment commenced` IS `the day my employment commenced`
            `er4 day the person becomes eligible to claim benefits under the plan` IS `the day I become eligible to claim benefits under my plan`
            `er4 day the person has an accumulation of 400 hours of active employment` IS `the day I have an accumulation of 400 hours of active employment`
            `er4 plan requires an elimination period` IS `my plan requires an elimination period`
            `er4 days in the elimination period` IS `the days in my plan's elimination period`
            `er4 elimination period begins with the first day of the period of incapacity` IS `the elimination period begins with the first day of my incapacity`
            `er4 plan pays in full whatever benefits are payable under the Act` IS `my plan pays in full whatever I am paid under the Act`
            `er4 plan pays in full whatever benefits are payable from another source that are not earnings under section 35` IS `my plan pays in full whatever I am paid from another source that is not earnings`
            `er4 weekly benefit payable under the plan` IS `the weekly benefit my plan pays me`
            `er4 normal weekly insurable earnings` IS `my normal weekly insurable earnings`
            `er4 active employment after which full benefits are reinstated on a recurrence` IS `the active employment after which my full benefits are reinstated when the illness recurs`
            `er4 active employment after which full benefits are reinstated for a new illness or injury` IS `the active employment after which my full benefits are reinstated for a new illness`
            `er4 longest period for which benefits are paid for one illness or injury, in weeks` IS `the longest period my plan pays benefits for one illness or injury, in weeks`
            `er4 events that end payment of benefits` IS `my events`
            `er4 conditions that preclude payment of benefits` IS `my conditions`
        `my special weekly indemnity case` MEANS `er4 Case under a Special Weekly Indemnity Plan` WITH
            `er4 section 63 case of the special plan` IS `my section 63 case`
            `er4 employer that provides or finances the special plan` IS `the employer providing or financing my plan`
            `er4 active employment after which full benefits are reinstated under the special plan, in months` IS `the active employment after which my full benefits are reinstated for a new illness`
            `er4 longest period for which the special plan pays benefits for one illness or injury, in weeks` IS `the longest period my plan pays benefits for one illness or injury, in weeks`
            `er4 events that end payment of benefits under the special plan` IS `my events`
        `my cumulative case` MEANS `er4 Case under a Cumulative Paid Sick Leave Plan` WITH
            `er4 section 63 case of the cumulative plan` IS `my section 63 case`
            `er4 cumulative plan credits only after the period or the hours referred to in paragraph 63(a)` IS `my plan credits only after the period or the hours in paragraph 63(a)`
            `er4 days of paid sick leave credited by the cumulative plan for each subsequent full month of active employment` IS `the days of paid sick leave my plan credits for each full month`
            `er4 days each month that the cumulative plan makes available only for illness or injury, pregnancy, child care or care or support of a family member` IS `the days each month my plan keeps for illness, injury, pregnancy, child care or care of a family member`
            `er4 months for which the cumulative plan defers eligibility to use paid sick leave` IS `the months for which my plan defers my eligibility to use paid sick leave`
            `er4 cumulative plan accumulates unused days at the rate in paragraphs 65(b) and (c)` IS `my plan lets unused days accumulate at the credited rate`
            `er4 maximum working days of paid sick leave the cumulative plan lets a person accumulate` IS `the most working days of paid sick leave my plan lets me accumulate`
            `er4 longest period for which the cumulative plan pays benefits for one illness or injury, in working days` IS `the longest period my plan pays benefits for one illness or injury, in working days`
            `er4 events that end payment of benefits under the cumulative plan` IS `my events`
        -- For an enhanced plan the same answers describe the plan, read against the enhanced requirements; the embedded
        -- cumulative case is read by reg 66(a) only for 65(a) and 65(d).
        `my enhanced case` MEANS `er4 Case under an Enhanced Cumulative Paid Sick Leave Plan` WITH
            `er4 section 65 case of the enhanced plan` IS `my cumulative case`
            `er4 enhanced plan credits only after the period or the hours referred to in paragraph 63(a)` IS `my plan credits only after the period or the hours in paragraph 63(a)`
            `er4 days of paid sick leave credited by the enhanced plan for each subsequent full month of active employment` IS `the days of paid sick leave my plan credits for each full month`
            `er4 days each month that the enhanced plan makes available only for illness or injury, pregnancy, child care or care or support of a family member` IS `the days each month my plan keeps for illness, injury, pregnancy, child care or care of a family member`
            `er4 enhanced plan accumulates unused days at the rate in paragraphs 66(b) and (c)` IS `my plan lets unused days accumulate at the credited rate`
            `er4 maximum working days of paid sick leave the enhanced plan lets a person accumulate` IS `the most working days of paid sick leave my plan lets me accumulate`
            `er4 longest period for which the enhanced plan pays benefits for one illness or injury, in working days` IS `the longest period my plan pays benefits for one illness or injury, in working days`
            `er4 events that end payment of benefits under the enhanced plan` IS `my events`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 69(1)
@export Which category of insured persons am I placed in on my employer's application (reg 69(1))?
GIVEN `the kind of my employer's plan` IS A `er4 Kind of wage-loss plan` @desc Which kind of plan is it: a Weekly Indemnity Plan, a Special Weekly Indemnity Plan, a Cumulative Paid Sick Leave Plan, an Enhanced Cumulative Paid Sick Leave Plan, or another wage-loss plan?
      `my employer's plan satisfies the requirements of the section for its kind` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the plan satisfy the requirements of regulation 63, 64, 65 or 66 for its kind?
      `my eligibility to use paid sick leave is deferred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your eligibility to use paid sick leave deferred as a temporary or probationary employee under paragraph 65(d)?
GIVETH A `er4 Category of insured persons`
DECIDE `Which category of insured persons am I placed in on my employer's application` IS
    `reg 69(1) the category the insured person is placed in`
        `the kind of my employer's plan` `my employer's plan satisfies the requirements of the section for its kind` `my eligibility to use paid sick leave is deferred`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 71
@export From what date does my employer's premium reduction take effect (reg 71)?
GIVEN `this is my employer's first application for the reduction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this your employer's first (initial) application for a reduction, rather than an application to continue one after the plan was modified or replaced?
      `the day my employer applied` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your employer make the application (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-03-16)?
      `the day my employer's plan was modified or replaced` IS A DATE @desc For a continuation: on what day did the plan's modification or replacement take effect (ISO 8601; any date if this is the first application)?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `From what date does my employer's premium reduction take effect` IS
    `reg 71 the effective date of the reduction of the employer's premium rate`
        `this is my employer's first application for the reduction` `the day my employer applied` `the day my employer's plan was modified or replaced`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 67(3)
@export Is my employer's plan a qualifying plan (reg 67(3))?
GIVEN `the kind of my employer's plan` IS A `er4 Kind of wage-loss plan` @desc Which kind of plan is it: a Weekly Indemnity Plan, a Special Weekly Indemnity Plan, a Cumulative Paid Sick Leave Plan, an Enhanced Cumulative Paid Sick Leave Plan, or another wage-loss plan?
      `my plan is set out in a formal written commitment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the plan set out in a formal written commitment (a union or association agreement, an industry-wide plan, an insurance policy, an undertaking in an employees' handbook or personnel policy bulletin, a board resolution, or a memorandum to employees)?
      `the commitment is only a board of directors' resolution that has not been implemented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only commitment a board of directors' resolution that has not been implemented?
      `my employer's plan meets the requirements of the section for its kind` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the plan meet the requirements of regulation 63, 64, 65 or 66 for its kind?
      `each insured person is credited as subsection 67(5) requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a paid sick leave plan: is each insured person covered credited with 72 days (cumulative plan) or 120 days (enhanced plan) of paid sick leave, less the days they could have accumulated since the plan began or in the six preceding years, whichever period is shorter?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my employer's plan a qualifying plan` IS
    `reg 67(3) the plan is a qualifying plan`
        `the kind of my employer's plan`
        (`reg 67(1) the plan is evidenced by a formal written commitment` `my commitments`)
        `my employer's plan meets the requirements of the section for its kind`
        `each insured person is credited as subsection 67(5) requires`
    WHERE
        `my commitments` MEANS
            IF NOT `my plan is set out in a formal written commitment` THEN EMPTY
            ELSE IF `the commitment is only a board of directors' resolution that has not been implemented`
                 THEN LIST (`er4 a board of directors' resolution` FALSE)
                 ELSE LIST `er4 another formal written commitment`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 67(2), reg 67(4), reg 71
@export For how many months of the year does my employer's premium reduction apply (reg 67(2), reg 67(4), reg 71)?
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER @desc For which year (for example 2026)?
      `the day my employer's plan became a qualifying plan` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the plan become a qualifying plan (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-03-16)?
      `my employer's plan has stopped being a qualifying plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the plan stopped being a qualifying plan?
      `the day my employer's plan stopped being a qualifying plan` IS A DATE @desc If it has stopped: on what day (ISO 8601; any date if it has not)?
      `this is my employer's first application for the reduction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this your employer's first (initial) application for a reduction, rather than an application to continue one?
      `the day my employer applied` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your employer make the application (ISO 8601)?
      `the day my employer's plan was modified or replaced` IS A DATE @desc For a continuation: on what day did the modification or replacement take effect (ISO 8601; any date if this is the first application)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `For how many months of the year does my employer's premium reduction apply` IS
    `reg 67(2) the number of months in the year to which the reduction applies`
        `the year`
        (`reg 67(4) the day on which a plan is considered to become or cease to be a qualifying plan` `the day my employer's plan became a qualifying plan`)
        (IF `my employer's plan has stopped being a qualifying plan`
         THEN JUST (`reg 67(4) the day on which a plan is considered to become or cease to be a qualifying plan` `the day my employer's plan stopped being a qualifying plan`)
         ELSE NOTHING)
        (`reg 71 the effective date of the reduction of the employer's premium rate`
            `this is my employer's first application for the reduction` `the day my employer applied` `the day my employer's plan was modified or replaced`)

§ `Parts III.1 and III.2 -- am I barred from federal benefits because I can receive provincial benefits?`

-- Situation: only for a person who lives where a province pays its own benefits for pregnancy or the care of a new-born or
-- adopted child (such as Quebec's QPIP), or whose partner does. "Provincial benefits" are those benefits; the question
-- "Are you self-employed?" (and, for fishers, claiming under the Fishing Regulations) picks the Part that applies.

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations regs 76.01, 76.31
@export Are the benefits I am paid provincial benefits within the meaning of these Regulations (regs 76.01, 76.31)?
GIVEN `I am self-employed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a self-employed person?
      `they are paid to me under a provincial plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the allowances, money or other benefits paid to you under a plan established under a provincial law?
      `they are paid because of my pregnancy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they paid because of your pregnancy?
      `they are paid for the care of my new-born child or children` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they paid in respect of your care of one or more of your new-born children?
      `they are paid for the care of a child placed with me for adoption` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they paid in respect of your care of one or more children placed with you for the purpose of adoption?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are the benefits I am paid provincial benefits within the meaning of these Regulations` IF
    IF `I am self-employed`
    THEN `reg 76.31 provincial benefits of a self-employed person`
             `they are paid to me under a provincial plan` `they are paid because of my pregnancy`
             `they are paid for the care of my new-born child or children` `they are paid for the care of a child placed with me for adoption`
    ELSE `reg 76.01 provincial benefits`
             `they are paid to me under a provincial plan` `they are paid because of my pregnancy`
             `they are paid for the care of my new-born child or children` `they are paid for the care of a child placed with me for adoption`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations regs 76.01, 76.31
@export Is my province's plan a plan to which these Regulations apply (regs 76.01, 76.31)?
GIVEN `I am self-employed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a self-employed person?
      `it is established under a provincial law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the plan established under a provincial law?
      `it provides for the payment of provincial benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it provide for the payment of benefits because of pregnancy or the care of a new-born or adopted child?
      `there is an agreement with the Government of Canada to reduce premiums` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there an agreement between the Government of Canada and the province to establish a system for reducing premiums where the plan's benefits would reduce or eliminate the federal benefits (employer's and employee's premiums if you are employed; the self-employment premium if you are self-employed)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my province's plan a plan to which these Regulations apply` IF
    IF `I am self-employed`
    THEN `reg 76.31 plan established under a provincial law`
             `it is established under a provincial law` `it provides for the payment of provincial benefits` `there is an agreement with the Government of Canada to reduce premiums`
    ELSE `reg 76.01 provincial plan`
             `it is established under a provincial law` `it provides for the payment of provincial benefits` `there is an agreement with the Government of Canada to reduce premiums`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations regs 76.09(1), 76.09(2), 76.36(1), 76.36(2)
@export Am I disentitled to maternity or parental benefits because I can receive provincial benefits (regs 76.09(1), 76.09(2), 76.36(1), 76.36(2))?
GIVEN `I am self-employed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a self-employed person (claiming under Part VII.1 of the Act, sections 152.04 and 152.05)?
      `I am entitled to receive provincial benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to receive provincial benefits under a provincial plan (even if you have since moved to another province)?
      `I asked the Commission to determine whether the provincial benefits are substantially equivalent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you ask the Commission to determine whether your provincial benefits are substantially equivalent to or greater than the federal benefits?
      `the Commission found the provincial amount not substantially equivalent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Commission determine that the provincial amount is not substantially equivalent to or greater than the amount of federal benefits you are entitled to?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I disentitled to maternity or parental benefits because I can receive provincial benefits` IF
    IF `I am self-employed`
    THEN `reg 76.36(1) the self-employed person is disentitled to be paid benefits under section 152.04 or 152.05 of the Act`
             `I am entitled to receive provincial benefits`
             (`reg 76.36(2) subsection (1) does not apply` `I asked the Commission to determine whether the provincial benefits are substantially equivalent` `the Commission found the provincial amount not substantially equivalent`)
    ELSE `reg 76.09(1) the claimant is disentitled to be paid benefits under section 22 or 23 of the Act`
             `I am entitled to receive provincial benefits`
             (`reg 76.09(2) subsection (1) does not apply` `I asked the Commission to determine whether the provincial benefits are substantially equivalent` `the Commission found the provincial amount not substantially equivalent`)

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations regs 76.09(4), 76.36(4)
@export Am I still caught by the provincial benefit rules if I have moved to another province (regs 76.09(4), 76.36(4))?
GIVEN `I am self-employed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a self-employed person?
      `I applied for provincial benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you apply for provincial benefits under a provincial plan?
      `I am entitled to receive them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to receive them?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I still caught by the provincial benefit rules if I have moved to another province` IF
    IF `I am self-employed`
    THEN `reg 76.36(4) subsections (1) to (3) apply to the self-employed person whether or not they have ceased to reside in the province providing those benefits` `I applied for provincial benefits` `I am entitled to receive them`
    ELSE `reg 76.09(4) subsections (1) to (3) apply to the claimant whether or not they have ceased to reside in the province where the plan was established` `I applied for provincial benefits` `I am entitled to receive them`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.09(3)
@export Am I disentitled to a week of other benefits, or of fishing benefits, because I received provincial benefits for that week (reg 76.09(3))?
GIVEN `the benefits I am claiming` IS A `er4 Benefits claimed by a claimant with provincial benefits` @desc Which benefits are you claiming: maternity (section 22), parental (section 23), other benefits under Part I of the Act, benefits under the Employment Insurance (Fishing) Regulations, or benefits of another kind?
      `I received, or applied for and am entitled to, provincial benefits for that week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For the week in question, have you received provincial benefits, or applied for them and are you entitled to them?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I disentitled to a week of other benefits, or of fishing benefits, because I received provincial benefits for that week` IS
    `reg 76.09(3) the claimant is disentitled to be paid those benefits in respect of the same week` `the benefits I am claiming` `I received, or applied for and am entitled to, provincial benefits for that week`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.36(3)
@export As a self-employed person, am I disentitled to a week of other benefits because I received provincial benefits for that week (reg 76.36(3))?
GIVEN `the benefits I am claiming` IS A `er4 Benefits claimed by a self-employed person with provincial benefits` @desc Which benefits are you claiming: maternity (section 152.04), parental (section 152.05), other benefits under Part VII.1 of the Act, or benefits of another kind?
      `I received, or applied for and am entitled to, provincial benefits for that week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For the week in question, have you received provincial benefits, or applied for them and are you entitled to them?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As a self-employed person, am I disentitled to a week of other benefits because I received provincial benefits for that week` IS
    `reg 76.36(3) the self-employed person is disentitled to be paid those benefits in respect of the same week` `the benefits I am claiming` `I received, or applied for and am entitled to, provincial benefits for that week`

-- Situation: only for a person who is caring for a child with another person (a partner, say) who may claim provincial
-- benefits. "The other person" is the one caring for the same child.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations regs 76.09(5), 76.36(5)
@export Am I disentitled because the other person caring for our child is entitled to provincial benefits (regs 76.09(5), 76.36(5))?
GIVEN `I am self-employed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a self-employed person?
      `the other person is self-employed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the other person caring for the child a self-employed person?
      `we are caring for the same child or children` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you and the other person caring for the same child or children?
      `the other person has applied for and is entitled to provincial benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the other person applied for provincial benefits and are they entitled to receive them?
      `I asked the Commission to determine whether the provincial benefits are substantially equivalent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you ask the Commission to determine whether the provincial benefits are substantially equivalent to or greater than your federal benefits?
      `the Commission found the provincial amount not substantially equivalent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Commission determine that the provincial amount is not substantially equivalent to or greater than your federal benefits?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I disentitled because the other person caring for our child is entitled to provincial benefits` IF
    IF `I am self-employed`
    THEN `reg 76.36(1) the self-employed person is disentitled to be paid benefits under section 152.04 or 152.05 of the Act`
             `the rules bind me`
             (`reg 76.36(2) subsection (1) does not apply` `I asked the Commission to determine whether the provincial benefits are substantially equivalent` `the Commission found the provincial amount not substantially equivalent`)
    ELSE `reg 76.09(1) the claimant is disentitled to be paid benefits under section 22 or 23 of the Act`
             `the rules bind me`
             (`reg 76.09(2) subsection (1) does not apply` `I asked the Commission to determine whether the provincial benefits are substantially equivalent` `the Commission found the provincial amount not substantially equivalent`)
    WHERE
        -- Four routes, by who is self-employed: 76.09(5)(a) (both insured), 76.09(5)(b) (I am self-employed, the other is not),
        -- 76.36(5)(b) (I am insured, the other is self-employed), 76.36(5)(a) (both self-employed). "The other person ... is a
        -- claimant referred to in subsection (4)" is read as having applied for and being entitled to provincial benefits.
        `the rules bind me` MEANS
            BRANCH IF (NOT `I am self-employed`) AND (NOT `the other person is self-employed`)
                     THEN `reg 76.09(5)(a) subsections (1) to (3) apply in respect of the other person` `we are caring for the same child or children` `the other person has applied for and is entitled to provincial benefits` TRUE
                   IF `I am self-employed` AND (NOT `the other person is self-employed`)
                     THEN `reg 76.09(5)(b) subsections 76.36(1) to (3) apply in respect of the other person` `we are caring for the same child or children` `the other person has applied for and is entitled to provincial benefits` TRUE
                   IF (NOT `I am self-employed`) AND `the other person is self-employed`
                     THEN `reg 76.36(5)(b) subsections 76.09(1) to (3) apply in respect of the other person` `we are caring for the same child or children` `the other person has applied for and is entitled to provincial benefits` TRUE
                   OTHERWISE `reg 76.36(5)(a) subsections (1) to (3) apply in respect of the other person` `we are caring for the same child or children` `the other person has applied for and is entitled to provincial benefits` TRUE

§ `Parts III.1 and III.2 -- how provincial benefits affect my claim and my weeks`

-- Situation: only for a person who has been, or is entitled to be, paid provincial benefits.

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.11
@export Am I an insured participant for employment benefits assistance (reg 76.11)?
GIVEN `I am already an insured participant under section 58 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you already an insured participant under section 58 of the Act?
      `I request assistance under employment benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an insured person who requests assistance under employment benefits?
      `I am unemployed when I request it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an unemployed person when you request the assistance?
      `I have a benefit period under a provincial plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a benefit period established under a provincial plan?
      `my benefit period under a provincial plan ended on` IS A DATE @desc If your provincial benefit period has ended: on what day (ISO 8601; any date if it has not)?
      `my provincial benefit period has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your benefit period under a provincial plan ended?
      `the day I request the assistance` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you request the assistance (ISO 8601)?
      `I would have had special benefits but for the provincial benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would you have been entitled to special benefits under section 22 or 23 had you not been entitled to provincial benefits?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I an insured participant for employment benefits assistance` IF
    `reg 76.11 the person is an insured participant, as the definition in section 58 of the Act is adapted`
        `I am already an insured participant under section 58 of the Act` `I request assistance under employment benefits` `I am unemployed when I request it`
        `I have a benefit period under a provincial plan`
        (IF `my provincial benefit period has ended` THEN JUST `my benefit period under a provincial plan ended on` ELSE NOTHING)
        `the day I request the assistance` `I would have had special benefits but for the provincial benefits`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.13
@export Does a week I was paid provincial benefits count as a week in receipt of benefits when my qualifying period is extended (reg 76.13)?
GIVEN `I was in receipt of benefits in the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you in receipt of EI benefits in that week?
      `I was paid provincial benefits in the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you paid provincial benefits in that week?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does a week I was paid provincial benefits count as a week in receipt of benefits when my qualifying period is extended` IF
    `reg 76.13 the week is a week during which the person was in receipt of benefits, for subsection 8(5) of the Act` `I was in receipt of benefits in the week` `I was paid provincial benefits in the week`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.14(a)
@export Do my benefits count as paid for pregnancy or the care of a new-born when my benefit period is extended (reg 76.14(a))?
GIVEN `the reason for the benefits` IS A `Reason for benefits` @desc For which reason were the benefits paid?
      `they were paid under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were they paid under the Employment Insurance Act?
      `they were provincial benefits paid for the same reason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were they provincial benefits paid for the same reason?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do my benefits count as paid for pregnancy or the care of a new-born when my benefit period is extended` IF
    `reg 76.14(a) the benefits count as benefits paid for one of the reasons mentioned in paragraphs 12(3)(a) and (b) of the Act` `the reason for the benefits` `they were paid under the Act` `they were provincial benefits paid for the same reason`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.14(b)
@export Up to how many weeks is my benefit period extended so that my other special benefits can be paid (reg 76.14(b))?
GIVEN `the reason for my other special benefits` IS A `Reason for benefits` @desc For which reason are you claiming the other special benefits?
      `the applicable maximum number of weeks for that reason` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the applicable maximum number of weeks for that reason under section 12(3) of the Act?
      `that maximum total number of weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum total number of weeks referred to in subsection 10(13) of the Act?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Up to how many weeks is my benefit period extended so that my other special benefits can be paid` IS
    `reg 76.14(b) the number of weeks up to which the benefit period is extended so that those benefits may be paid`
        `the reason for my other special benefits` `the applicable maximum number of weeks for that reason` `that maximum total number of weeks`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.15
@export By how many weeks is my benefit period extended because my child was in hospital (reg 76.15)?
GIVEN `I have received or am entitled to receive provincial benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you received, or are you entitled to receive, provincial benefits?
      `the weeks my child or children were in hospital in the period` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many weeks was your child or were your children hospitalized during the period referred to in subsection 23(2) of the Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `By how many weeks is my benefit period extended because my child was in hospital` IS
    `reg 76.15 the number of weeks by which the benefit period is considered to be extended under subsection 10(12) of the Act`
        `I have received or am entitled to receive provincial benefits` `the weeks my child or children were in hospital in the period`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations regs 76.16, 76.17, 76.37, 76.38
@export How much will my benefits for a week be after the provincial benefits are deducted, in dollars (regs 76.16, 76.17, 76.37, 76.38)?
GIVEN `I am self-employed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a self-employed person?
      `I received or am entitled to provincial benefits for that week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For the week in question, have you received, or are you entitled to receive, provincial benefits?
      `my benefits for the week after the other deductions` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your federal benefits for the week, in dollars, after the other deductions the Act makes (earnings, and so on)?
      `my provincial benefits for the week` IS A NUMBER @desc What provincial benefits have you received, or are you entitled to receive, for the same week, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much will my benefits for a week be after the provincial benefits are deducted` IS
    IF NOT `I received or am entitled to provincial benefits for that week`
    THEN JUST `my benefits for the week after the other deductions`
    ELSE IF `I am self-employed`
         THEN `reg 76.38 the benefits payable under section 152.04 or 152.05 of the Act for the week after the provincial benefits are deducted` `my benefits for the week after the other deductions` `my provincial benefits for the week`
         ELSE `reg 76.17 the benefits payable under section 22 or 23 of the Act for the week after the provincial benefits are deducted` `my benefits for the week after the other deductions` `my provincial benefits for the week`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations regs 76.18, 76.39
@export May a week of my EI benefits be counted for a purpose when a week of my provincial benefits has already been counted for it (regs 76.18, 76.39)?
GIVEN `I am self-employed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a self-employed person?
      `a week of my provincial benefits has already been counted for that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a week of your provincial benefits already been taken into account for the purpose (regulations 76.11 to 76.14 and 76.19 for an employed person; regulation 76.4 for a self-employed person)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May a week of my EI benefits be counted for a purpose when a week of my provincial benefits has already been counted for it` IF
    IF `I am self-employed`
    THEN `reg 76.39 benefits paid under section 152.04 or 152.05 of the Act in respect of a week may be taken into account for that same purpose` `a week of my provincial benefits has already been counted for that purpose`
    ELSE `reg 76.18 a week of benefits paid under section 22 or 23 of the Act may be taken into account for that same purpose` `a week of my provincial benefits has already been counted for that purpose`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations regs 76.19(1), 76.4(1)
@export How many weeks of benefits are left within my maximum once my provincial weeks are counted (regs 76.19(1), 76.4(1))?
GIVEN `I am self-employed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a self-employed person?
      `the overall maximum number of weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the overall maximum number of weeks that apply to you (paragraphs 12(3)(a) and (b), or 152.14(1)(a) and (b), of the Act taken together)?
      `the weeks of benefits I was paid under the Act` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of benefits have you been paid under the Act?
      `the weeks of provincial benefits I was paid` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of provincial benefits have you been paid (convert weeks paid at an accelerated rate using the question on accelerated weeks)?
      `I would have been entitled to the corresponding benefits under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would you have been entitled to the corresponding types of benefits under the Act for those weeks?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many weeks of benefits are left within my maximum once my provincial weeks are counted` IS
    IF `I am self-employed`
    THEN `reg 76.4(1)(a) the weeks left within the overall maximum` `the overall maximum number of weeks` `the weeks of benefits I was paid under the Act` `the provincial weeks that count`
    ELSE `reg 76.19(1)(a) the weeks left within the overall maximum` `the overall maximum number of weeks` `the weeks of benefits I was paid under the Act` `the provincial weeks that count`
    WHERE
        -- Provincial weeks count as weeks under the Act "if the claimant would have been entitled to the corresponding types of benefits".
        `the provincial weeks that count` MEANS
            IF (IF `I am self-employed`
                THEN `reg 76.4(1) the provincial benefits paid for the week are considered to be benefits paid in respect of a week under the Act` `I would have been entitled to the corresponding benefits under the Act`
                ELSE `reg 76.19(1) the provincial benefits paid for the week are considered to be benefits paid in respect of a week under the Act` `I would have been entitled to the corresponding benefits under the Act`)
            THEN `the weeks of provincial benefits I was paid`
            ELSE 0

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations regs 76.19(2), 76.19(3), 76.4(3), 76.4(4)
@export How many weeks of benefits do my provincial weeks, paid at an accelerated rate, represent (regs 76.19(2), 76.19(3), 76.4(3), 76.4(4))?
GIVEN `I am self-employed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a self-employed person?
      `I was paid the provincial benefits at the accelerated rate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you paid the provincial benefits at an accelerated rate (the maximum amount paid over fewer weeks)?
      `the weeks of that type of provincial benefits I was paid` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of that type of provincial benefits were you paid?
      `the maximum weeks of that type at the non-accelerated rate` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum number of weeks of that type of benefit payable at the non-accelerated rate?
      `the maximum weeks of that type at the accelerated rate` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum number of weeks of that type of benefit payable at the accelerated rate?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many weeks of benefits do my provincial weeks, paid at an accelerated rate, represent` IS
    IF `I am self-employed`
    THEN `reg 76.4(3) and (4) the weeks of provincial benefits as weeks under the Act` `I was paid the provincial benefits at the accelerated rate` `the weeks of that type of provincial benefits I was paid` `the maximum weeks of that type at the non-accelerated rate` `the maximum weeks of that type at the accelerated rate`
    ELSE `reg 76.19(2) and (3) the weeks of provincial benefits as weeks under the Act` `I was paid the provincial benefits at the accelerated rate` `the weeks of that type of provincial benefits I was paid` `the maximum weeks of that type at the non-accelerated rate` `the maximum weeks of that type at the accelerated rate`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations regs 76.2, 76.41
@export How many of my provincial weeks are taken into account when the provincial plan allows more weeks than the Act (regs 76.2, 76.41)?
GIVEN `I am self-employed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a self-employed person?
      `the maximum number of weeks the Act allows for that reason` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum number of weeks the Act allows for that reason (paragraph 12(3)(a) or (b) or (4)(a) or (b), or 152.14(1)(a) or (b) or (2)(a) or (b))?
      `the maximum number of weeks the provincial plan allows` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum number of weeks for which the corresponding provincial benefits may be paid?
      `the weeks of provincial benefits I was paid` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of provincial benefits have you been paid?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many of my provincial weeks are taken into account when the provincial plan allows more weeks than the Act` IS
    IF `I am self-employed`
    THEN `reg 76.41 the weeks of provincial benefits that are taken into account in determining the maximum number of weeks` `the maximum number of weeks the Act allows for that reason` `the maximum number of weeks the provincial plan allows` `the weeks of provincial benefits I was paid`
    ELSE `reg 76.2 the weeks of provincial benefits that are taken into account in determining the maximum number of weeks` `the maximum number of weeks the Act allows for that reason` `the maximum number of weeks the provincial plan allows` `the weeks of provincial benefits I was paid`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations regs 76.19(1.1), 76.4(2)
@export When is my benefit period deemed to have begun when I had a benefit period under a provincial law (regs 76.19(1.1), 76.4(2))?
GIVEN `I am self-employed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a self-employed person?
      `a benefit period was established for me under a provincial law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a benefit period established for you under a provincial law?
      `the first week of that provincial benefit period` IS A DATE @desc What was the first week of that provincial benefit period (ISO 8601 date of the week)?
      `I would have been entitled to the corresponding benefits for the same period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would you have been entitled to the corresponding types of benefits under the Act in respect of the same period?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `When is my benefit period deemed to have begun when I had a benefit period under a provincial law` IS
    IF `I am self-employed`
    THEN `reg 76.4(2) the week in which the benefit period is deemed to have begun` `a benefit period was established for me under a provincial law` `the first week of that provincial benefit period` `I would have been entitled to the corresponding benefits for the same period`
    ELSE `reg 76.19(1.1) the week in which the benefit period is deemed to have begun` `a benefit period was established for me under a provincial law` `the first week of that provincial benefit period` `I would have been entitled to the corresponding benefits for the same period`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations regs 76.21, 76.42
@export How many weeks of parental benefits can I be paid when the other parent claims provincial benefits (regs 76.21, 76.42)?
GIVEN `I am self-employed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a self-employed person (claiming under section 152.05 of the Act)?
      `we are caring for the same child or children` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you and the other parent caring for the same child or children?
      `we do not live in the same province when the first of us applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you and the other parent live in different provinces when the first of you made an application?
      `the weeks I would otherwise be entitled to` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of parental benefits would you otherwise be entitled to under the Act?
      `the other parent applied first` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the other parent (the provincial applicant) make the earlier application? (No, if you applied first.)
      `we agreed on the weeks or a court ordered how to share them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you and the other parent agreed on the number of weeks each will apply for, or is there a court order about sharing the weeks?
      `my election` IS A `Election of maximum weeks` @desc Which maximum did you elect: the 35-week maximum or the 61-week maximum?
      `A, the maximum weeks when the weeks are divided` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum number of weeks when the weeks of benefits are divided, under subparagraph 12(4)(b)(i) (or 152.14(2)(b)(i)) of the Act?
      `B, the weeks of provincial benefits paid to the other parent` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of provincial benefits were paid to the other parent (weeks paid at an accelerated rate converted as the Regulations say)?
      `C, the maximum weeks of the 61-week election` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum number of weeks under subparagraph 12(3)(b)(ii) (or 152.14(1)(b)(ii)) of the Act?
      `D, the maximum weeks of the 35-week election` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum number of weeks under subparagraph 12(3)(b)(i) (or 152.14(1)(b)(i)) of the Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many weeks of parental benefits can I be paid when the other parent claims provincial benefits` IS
    IF NOT (IF `I am self-employed`
            THEN `reg 76.42(1) subsection (2) applies in respect of the two persons` `we are caring for the same child or children` `we do not live in the same province when the first of us applies`
            ELSE `reg 76.21(1) subsection (2) applies in respect of the two persons` `we are caring for the same child or children` `we do not live in the same province when the first of us applies`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `I am self-employed`
         THEN `reg 76.42 the number of weeks of benefits payable to the self-employed person`
                  `the weeks I would otherwise be entitled to` `who applied first` `we agreed on the weeks or a court ordered how to share them` `my election`
                  `A, the maximum weeks when the weeks are divided` `B, the weeks of provincial benefits paid to the other parent` `C, the maximum weeks of the 61-week election` `D, the maximum weeks of the 35-week election`
         ELSE `reg 76.21 the number of weeks of benefits payable to the claimant`
                  `the weeks I would otherwise be entitled to` `who applied first` `we agreed on the weeks or a court ordered how to share them` `my election`
                  `A, the maximum weeks when the weeks are divided` `B, the weeks of provincial benefits paid to the other parent` `C, the maximum weeks of the 61-week election` `D, the maximum weeks of the 35-week election`
    WHERE
        `who applied first` MEANS
            IF `the other parent applied first`
            THEN `er4 the provincial applicant made the earlier application`
            ELSE `er4 the person claiming benefits under the Act made the earlier application`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations regs 76.22, 76.421
@export Is my waiting period waived because provincial benefits were paid to me (regs 76.22, 76.421)?
GIVEN `I am self-employed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a self-employed person?
      `sick leave pay was payable to me by my employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were allowances, payments or other moneys payable to you by your employer or former employer as sick leave pay?
      `provincial benefits were paid to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were provincial benefits paid to you?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my waiting period waived because provincial benefits were paid to me` IF
    IF `I am self-employed`
    THEN `reg 76.421 the condition of paragraph 40(6)(b), as adapted, is met` `sick leave pay was payable to me by my employer` `provincial benefits were paid to me`
    ELSE `reg 76.22 the condition of paragraph 40(6)(b), as adapted, is met` `sick leave pay was payable to me by my employer` `provincial benefits were paid to me`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.23
@export Does the Act as it stood before the provincial plan rules still apply to my claim (reg 76.23)?
GIVEN `the day my child was born or placed with me for adoption` IS A DATE @desc On what day was your child born, or placed with you for the purpose of adoption (ISO 8601)?
      `the day Part III.1 came into force` IS A DATE @desc On what day did Part III.1 of the Regulations come into force (ISO 8601)? The Regulations in this range do not give it.
      `the weeks of benefits I was paid before that day` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of benefits under section 22 or 23 of the Act had you been paid, for this birth or placement, before that day?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the Act as it stood before the provincial plan rules still apply to my claim` IF
    `reg 76.23 the Act applies to the claim as it did before this Part` `the day my child was born or placed with me for adoption` `the day Part III.1 came into force` `the weeks of benefits I was paid before that day`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.43
@export Am I deemed to meet the 12-month condition after moving out of a province with a plan (reg 76.43)?
GIVEN `the day I ceased to reside in that province` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you cease to reside in the province that has a plan established under a provincial law (ISO 8601)?
      `the day I entered into my agreement under section 152.02 of the Act` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you enter into your agreement under section 152.02 of the Act (ISO 8601)?
      `I was covered by that plan during the 12 months before I ceased to reside there` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you covered by that plan during the 12 months before the day you ceased to reside in the province?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I deemed to meet the 12-month condition after moving out of a province with a plan` IF
    `reg 76.43 the self-employed person is deemed to have satisfied the condition set out in paragraph 152.07(1)(a) of the Act`
        `the day I ceased to reside in that province` `the day I entered into my agreement under section 152.02 of the Act` `I was covered by that plan during the 12 months before I ceased to reside there`

§ `Parts III.1 and III.2 -- the premium I pay`

-- Situation: only for a person whose province has a plan that pays benefits for pregnancy or the care of a new-born or adopted
-- child, or who works in such a province.

DECLARE `er4 What the employer does about the provincial premium reduction at source` IS ONE OF
    `er4 the employer takes the premium reduction into account`
    `er4 the employer does not take the premium reduction into account`
    `er4 the Regulations do not say`

-- Regs 76.24 and 76.25 are the two special cases; 76.04 is the general rule that the premiums are reduced. A person covered by a
-- plan who works in a province with a plan is the ordinary case of reg 76.04. A person who is neither covered nor working in a
-- province with a plan is not mentioned by any of the three: "the Regulations do not say".
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations regs 76.04, 76.24, 76.25
@export Will my employer take the provincial premium reduction into account when deducting my premium (regs 76.04, 76.24, 76.25)?
GIVEN `where I am employed` IS A `er4 Where the insured person is employed` @desc Where are you employed: in a province that has a provincial plan, in a province that has no provincial plan, or outside Canada?
      `I am covered by a provincial plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you covered by a provincial plan (a plan paying benefits for pregnancy or the care of a new-born or adopted child)?
      `provincial benefits would reduce or eliminate my federal benefits under section 22 or 23` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the payment of provincial benefits to insured persons under the plan have the effect of reducing or eliminating the benefits payable under section 22 or 23 of the Act?
GIVETH A `er4 What the employer does about the provincial premium reduction at source`
DECIDE `Will my employer take the provincial premium reduction into account when deducting my premium` IS
    BRANCH IF `reg 76.24 the employer is not to take any premium reduction into account in deducting the employee's premium or remitting the employer's premium` `I am covered by a provincial plan` `where I am employed`
             THEN `er4 the employer does not take the premium reduction into account`
           IF `reg 76.25 the employer is to take any premium reduction into account in deducting the employee's premium and remitting the employer's premium` `I am covered by a provincial plan` `where I am employed`
             THEN `er4 the employer takes the premium reduction into account`
           IF     `I am covered by a provincial plan` AND `where I am employed` EQUALS `er4 in a province that has a provincial plan`
              AND `reg 76.04 the employee's and employer's premiums payable under sections 67 and 68 of the Act are to be reduced` `provincial benefits would reduce or eliminate my federal benefits under section 22 or 23`
             THEN `er4 the employer takes the premium reduction into account`
           OTHERWISE `er4 the Regulations do not say`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.33
@export As a self-employed person, is my self-employment premium reduced because of provincial benefits (reg 76.33)?
GIVEN `provincial benefits would reduce or eliminate my federal benefits under section 152.04 or 152.05` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the payment of provincial benefits have the effect of reducing or eliminating the benefits payable to you under section 152.04 or 152.05 of the Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As a self-employed person, is my self-employment premium reduced because of provincial benefits` IS
    `reg 76.33 the self-employment premium payable under section 152.21 of the Act is to be reduced` `provincial benefits would reduce or eliminate my federal benefits under section 152.04 or 152.05`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations regs 76.05, 76.34
@export By how much is my premium reduced, in dollars (regs 76.05, 76.34)?
GIVEN `I am self-employed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a self-employed person?
      `the amount my premium rate is applied to` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount to which your premium rate is applied, in dollars (your insurable earnings if you are employed; the earnings on which your self-employment premium is calculated if you are self-employed)?
      `the published premium reduction rate` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the published premium reduction rate, as a fraction (for example 0.0054 for 0.54%)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `By how much is my premium reduced` IS
    IF `I am self-employed`
    THEN `reg 76.34 the premium reduction to be applied to the self-employment premium` `the amount my premium rate is applied to` `the published premium reduction rate`
    ELSE `reg 76.05 the premium reduction obtained by applying the premium reduction rate` `the amount my premium rate is applied to` `the published premium reduction rate`

-- Situation: only for a person covered by a provincial plan who works in a province with no plan, or outside Canada (reg 76.24),
-- and who lived in the plan's province on 31 December.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.26(1)
@export How much premium adjustment is paid to my province on my behalf, in dollars (reg 76.26(1))?
GIVEN `I lived in that province on December 31 of the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you live in the province whose plan covers you on December 31 of the year?
      `the premium reduction deducted from my pay in the year` IS A NUMBER @desc How much premium reduction (as part of your employee's premiums) was deducted from your pay in the year, in dollars?
      `my overpayment of employee's premiums for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc How much did you overpay in employee's premiums under Part IV of the Act for the year, in dollars?
      `what I owe under the provincial plan for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc How much do you owe under the provincial plan for the year, in dollars?
      `the premium reduction my employers remitted as employer's premiums for me` IS A NUMBER @desc How much premium reduction did your employers remit as employer's premiums for you in the year, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much premium adjustment is paid to my province on my behalf` IS
    `reg 76.26(1) the premium adjustment that the Minister of National Revenue is to pay to the province` (LIST `me`)
    WHERE
        `me` MEANS `er4 Insured person referred to in section 76.24` WITH
            `er4 resides in the province on December 31 of the year` IS `I lived in that province on December 31 of the year`
            `er4 amounts deducted by employers in the year that represent the premium reduction, as or on account of employee's premiums` IS `the premium reduction deducted from my pay in the year`
            `er4 amounts representing an overpayment of employee's premiums under Part IV of the Act for the year` IS `my overpayment of employee's premiums for the year`
            `er4 amounts the insured person owes in the year under the provincial plan` IS `what I owe under the provincial plan for the year`
            `er4 amounts representing the premium reduction remitted by employers in the year as employer's premiums` IS `the premium reduction my employers remitted as employer's premiums for me`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.28(1)
@export What premiums are counted in deciding whether I overpaid, once my province's premium adjustment is added (reg 76.28(1))?
GIVEN `the employee's premiums deducted from my pay and paid under the Act` IS A NUMBER @desc How much in employee's premiums was deducted from your pay and paid under the Act, in dollars?
      `the premium adjustment my province has paid or must pay for premiums deducted under its plan` IS A NUMBER @desc How much premium adjustment has your province paid, or is it required to pay, to the Receiver General for the premiums deducted under its plan, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What premiums are counted in deciding whether I overpaid, once my province's premium adjustment is added` IS
    `reg 76.28(1) the employee's premiums taken into account in determining whether there has been an overpayment`
        `the employee's premiums deducted from my pay and paid under the Act` `the premium adjustment my province has paid or must pay for premiums deducted under its plan`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.28(2)
@export Is a premium adjustment paid to my province counted in deciding whether I overpaid (reg 76.28(2))?
GIVEN `the amount is a premium adjustment paid or to be paid to a province under reg 76.26(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the amount a premium adjustment referred to in subsection 76.26(1) that has been paid, or is required to be paid, to a province that has a provincial plan?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a premium adjustment paid to my province counted in deciding whether I overpaid` IF
    `reg 76.28(2) the amount is taken into account for the purposes of Part IV of the Act` `the amount is a premium adjustment paid or to be paid to a province under reg 76.26(1)`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations regs 76.3, 76.45
@export May the Canada Revenue Agency and the Minister of National Revenue disclose my information to my province (regs 76.3, 76.45)?
GIVEN `I am self-employed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a self-employed person?
      `my province has a plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your province have a provincial plan (for a self-employed person: a plan established under a provincial law)?
      `the information is necessary for administering Part III.1 or Part III.2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information necessary for the administration of that Part?
      `it was obtained under the Act or these Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it obtained by the Agency or the Minister under the Act or these Regulations, or prepared from information so obtained?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Canada Revenue Agency and the Minister of National Revenue disclose my information to my province` IF
    IF `I am self-employed`
    THEN `reg 76.45 the Canada Revenue Agency and the Minister of National Revenue are authorized to disclose the information to the province` `my province has a plan` `the information is necessary for administering Part III.1 or Part III.2` `it was obtained under the Act or these Regulations`
    ELSE `reg 76.3 the Canada Revenue Agency and the Minister of National Revenue are authorized to disclose the information to the province` `my province has a plan` `the information is necessary for administering Part III.1 or Part III.2` `it was obtained under the Act or these Regulations`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations regs 76.29, 76.44
@export Will my social insurance number be used to exchange information with my province (regs 76.29, 76.44)?
GIVEN `I am self-employed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a self-employed person?
      `the use is to exchange information between the Government of Canada and a province` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the number used to facilitate the exchange, between the Government of Canada and a province, of information obtained about you under provincial law or the Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will my social insurance number be used to exchange information with my province` IF
    IF `I am self-employed`
    THEN `reg 76.44 the self-employed person's social insurance number is to be used` `the use is to exchange information between the Government of Canada and a province`
    ELSE `reg 76.29 the claimant's social insurance number is to be used` `the use is to exchange information between the Government of Canada and a province`
